# The network of "The cloud link": the clinic's data centre and its cloud
# network, joined by a private circuit and, across the internet, a VPN.
#
#   dcapp 10.41.0.10 -- dc -- edge (AS 65040) ==dx 169.254.30.0/30== cloud (AS 65515) -- vpc -- vm 10.200.1.10
#                              \ 198.51.100.40 == inet == 203.0.113.40 /
#                               (the VPN: vti0 169.254.21.2 to 169.254.21.1, inside IPsec)
#
# dx stands in for a private circuit (Direct Connect, ExpressRoute or Cloud
# Interconnect): a cable with a BGP session over it. inet stands in for the
# internet: a router that knows only the two outside networks, so the data
# centre's traffic crosses it only inside the tunnel. cloud stands in for
# the cloud provider's side, its circuit router and VPN gateway in one
# (AS 65515, a private AS number, Azure's default for a VPN gateway), and isn't the learner's: its BGP, its IPsec connection and its
# end of the tunnel are scenery. edge is the data centre's router, the
# learner's: FRR runs with only a default route, and strongSwan with no
# connection. The data centre's four networks are four addresses on
# edge's LAN. The VPN's inside addresses are lower than the circuit's, so
# when nothing else tells two paths apart, BGP's last tie-breaker (the
# lowest neighbour address) picks the VPN: the lab can't be passed by
# leaving things as they are. Addresses come from the private ranges, the
# documentation ranges for the internet (RFC 5737), and the link-local
# block for the circuit and the tunnel's inside, as the clouds use.
machine dcapp
machine edge router
machine inet router
machine cloud router
machine vm

lan dc dcapp:eth0=10.41.0.10/24 edge:lan=10.40.0.1/24,10.41.0.1/24,10.42.0.1/24,10.43.0.1/24
link edge:dx=169.254.30.1/30 cloud:dx=169.254.30.2/30
link edge:wan=198.51.100.40/24 inet:edge=198.51.100.1/24
link inet:cloud=203.0.113.1/24 cloud:wan=203.0.113.40/24
lan vpc cloud:vpc=10.200.0.1/16 vm:eth0=10.200.1.10/16

route dcapp default via 10.41.0.1
route vm default via 10.200.0.1

# The provider's end of the tunnel. Key 5 is the mark that ties its vti0 to
# the IPsec SA whose mark_in and mark_out are 5 (cloud's swanctl file).
tunnel cloud vti0 vti local 203.0.113.40 remote 198.51.100.40 key 5 addr 169.254.21.1/30

run edge frr strongswan
run cloud frr strongswan
run dcapp web-svc
run vm web-svc
